# TTS Module — Build Notes & Wiring Roadmap
**Created:** March 2026  
**Status:** Stage 1 complete — manual operation, voice selected, wiring pending

---

## What We Built

A standalone Python TTS module (`cgen/scripts/tts_module.py`) that takes a script and renders it as audio. Intentionally built outside the pipeline so it can be pressure-tested manually before automation.

**Engine:** Kokoro (local, free, no API dependency)  
**Underlying model:** ContentVec / HuBERT-derived speech representations  
**Why Kokoro:** No vendor lock-in, runs on local GPU (RTX 3060 Ti), no per-minute cost, quality is competitive with paid APIs for narration use cases.

---

## How to Run It (Manual)

```bash
python cgen/scripts/tts_module.py --file "path/to/script.txt" --output "path/to/output.wav" --format wav --voice bf_emma --speed 1.0
```

**Input options:**
- `--file path` — .txt script or course.json
- `--paste` — interactive paste from terminal
- `--list-voices` — print available voices

**Output options:**
- `--format wav` — works out of the box
- `--format mp3` — requires pydub + ffmpeg (see known issues)

