## JSON Integration (How It Already Works)

The module already accepts `course.json` as input via `--file`. It walks the JSON tree looking for these keys:

```
narration, script, narrator_text, vo, voiceover, text
```

If your course.json schema uses different field names, update `TARGET_KEYS` in `extract_narration_from_json()` near the top of the script.

